1 NOTE He was the Parish Priest in Hitra, Norway from 1577 on. He was named as Church Warden on "Herredagen" (council of nobles) in Trondheim 1578. He was also called on to appear at "Herredagen" there in 1597. In 1610, he sought permiss
2 CONC ion from King Christian IV to live in Hemne Annex. He had, "for some time, lived at the king's property Kjørse in Hemne Annex and had built (houses) on it at his own expense, so now he found it most undesirable to have to live in 
2 CONC Hoved Sogn." He was a large landowner. He was apparently one of the largest exporters of lumber on the Møre coast. Gerhard Schøning says that the Dutch on their sea charts had "Herr Mikkel op Hemne."
1 NOTE T 1550 - 1618
2 CONT
