1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://research.frick.org/montias/details/1135
2 CONT
2 CONT Appelman, Sijmen
2 CONT
2 CONT ? |d 1631
2 CONT
2 CONT On the East side of the Breestraet in Amsterdam
2 CONT
2 CONT probably Remonstrant
2 CONT
2 CONT Inventaris ofte specificatie van de imboel ende huysraet achtergelaten bij wijlen Sijmen Appelman ... opt requisitie van Hendrick Helt gesubst. schout ende swager van de voors. overleden. Synde bevonden als volcht. Postscript: Ald
2 CONC us gedaen ende inventariseert ten huyse van den overleden ter presentie van de kinderen, erffgenamen van den selven overleden, opten 13e aprilis anno 1631.
2 CONT
2 CONT The address of the late Sijmen Appelman is taken from the 1631 Kohier. He paid a tax of 75 f. together with his swager (N.N. Stock ?) and lived on the East side of the Breestraet, beneath the Sluijs. Simon Appelman signed the Remo
2 CONC nstrant petition of 1611. He was the son of Balthasar Simonsz. Appelman, who was a member of the Amsterdam Vroedschap from 1578 to 1602 and the brother of Sijbrand Appelman (1573-1602). Simon Appelman, born in 1572, married Annetg
2 CONC e Claes Trebijn, daughter of Claes Trebijn and of Niesge Sijbrands Appelman in April 1600. Appelman was the brother-in-law of Hendrick Helt, substitue schout, but through what marriage is not known. He was buried on 22 November 16
2 CONC 30 (Elias, Vroedschap, p. 70).
2 CONT Notary Jacob Westfrisius
2 CONT
