1 NAME Hugh /Mackay/ 4th of Scoury
2 GIVN Hugh
2 SURN Mackay
2 NSFX 4th of Scoury
2 _MARNM Mackay
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1681
2 PLAC Willemstad, Ooststellingwerf, Friesland, Netherlands 
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1708
2 PLAC Breda, Noord-Brabant, Netherlands 
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} IV. Hugh, only son of General Mackay, was given a company in his father's Scots regiment, 1st September, 1692, and d. at Cambrai in 1708 of an accident received in the field, holding the rank of major. He m. Anna t
2 CONC ie Lancy, a Swiss lady, who bore him two sons and one dau. : —
2 CONT i. Hugh, of whom follows.
2 CONT
2 CONT ii. Gabriel, became captain in Halket's Scots regiment 20th November, 1730, colonel 1st April, 1748, and was dead in 1758 (Scots Brigade in Holland).
2 CONT
2 CONT iii. Clara Margaret, m. Baron Ren Duyck, and had issue :—
2 CONT * James Charles Ren Duyck, m. Baroness Louisa Neuvenherm, with issue ; and 
2 CONT * Anna, m. Major General J. W. Van der Hup, and had issue living in 1828 (Blk. MS.).
2 CONT
2 CONT p g. 290-291 THE BOOK OF MACKAY BY ANGUS MACKAY, M.A. (St. Andrews University)
2 CONT  Minister at Westerdale, Caithness EDINBURGH : NORMAN MACLEOD,  -25 GEORGE IV. BRIDGE CANADA : EDWARD MACKAY, ST. PETER'S MANSE,
2 CONT  MADOC, ONT. M DCCCC VI
2 CONT
2 CONT ==================================
2 CONT
2 CONT THE SCOWRY BRANCH OF MACKAYS.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hugh, who was major of his father's regiment, died at Cambray in 1708, aged about 25, leaving by his marriage with Anna de Lancy two sons, 
2 CONT * Hugh and 
2 CONT > Hugh died at Breda in 1775, a lieutenant-general in the Dutch service, and colonel of the Mackay Dutch regiment, leaving by his marriage with Isabella de Favinia, an only daughter, who married Lieutenant-general Prevost of the B
2 CONC ritish service, who, upon the death of his father-in-law without male issue, obtained the king's license to bear the name and arms of Mackay of Scowry, in addition to those of Prevost, which his descendants in Holland still bear  
2 CONT > General Prevost Mackay left two daughters of his marriage  above-mentioned ; the eldest of whom, 
2 CONT >>* Constantia, married Major Cornebie of a Walloon regiment, and had issue 
2 CONT * Gabriel , who was Lieutenant-colonel of the Mackay regiment, died without issue a daughter, 
2 CONT * Clara-Margaret. 
2 CONT >Clara-Margaret, daughter of Major Hugh, married Baron Ren Duyck, one of the nobles of Guelderland, and left issue, a son,
2 CONT >>* James-Charles Ren Duyck, who married Louise, Baroness Nuvenherm;
2 CONT > and a daughter, 
2 CONT >>* Anna, married to Major-general J. W. Vanderhup, both living at Numeguen with issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT Pg. 562-3  HISTORY THE HOUSE AND CLAN MACKAY,BY ROBERT MACKAY, 1829
