1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Links: Kåre Hasselberg research on Peter Dundas:
2 CONT
2 CONT The Dundases of Norway descends from an immigrated scotsman named Peter Dass or Dundas, who came from Dundee ca.1630 and settled down in Bergen, but later moved to Northern Norway and settled down permanently there. He had a siste
2 CONC r named Maria who married a Bergen merchant named Johan (Jan) Fasmer.
2 CONT
2 CONT One Peter Dundas is mentioned in 1562 in the Kirk Session register of St.Andrews , as his father Archibald Dundas in Pote (Pottey) was divorced from his wife Gelis Scrymgeour due to Archibald's adultery with two women. Peter was m
2 CONC ade responsible for bringing his father to the baillie of Abernethie (near Perth) and "underly civil correccione for the foyrsaidis crimis".   Maintland Club page 294
2 CONT
2 CONT Another Peter Dundas (or the same?) made February 4th, 1554 a contract with the curator of Thomas Hamilton of Priestfield, to lease the lands of Balvin in the sheriff-dom of Perth from Thomas Hamilton.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://archive.org/details/collectionsnotes00ball/page/12?q=Peter+Dundas
2 CONT
2 CONT  Archibald Dundas in Pote. He may perhaps be that "A.D. de Pottey", who is mentioned "in assize" in Edinburgh together with Alexander Dundas of Fingask June 3rd, 1540, and also in assize in Edinburgh April 19th, 1544. Both documen
2 CONC ts are found in Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, vol.III no.2156 and 3009). This may perhaps indicate a relationship to the Dundases of Fingask 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://archive.org/details/collectionsnotes00ball/page/12?q=Peter+Dundas
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.dundasfamily.co.uk/record_61.htm   
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Memorandum narrating that Andrew Rwen in Drone Estir appointed Sir john Leirmontht and Robert Leirmontht  his procurators to act him in the books of the commissaries of Dunblane to pay John Pitcarne in Dron the sum of 28 merks nam
2 CONC ely 14 merks at Martinmas next and other 14 merks at Whitsunday 1557, under pain of excommunication. Done in the cemetery of the marsh church of Abirnethy 19th April 1556.
2 CONT
2 CONT Witnesses, John Vemys of Pitgrunze, Sir Robert Laing, Peter Dundas and William Duncan.
2 CONT
2 CONT Protocol Book of Sir Alexander Gaw 1540-1558 https://archive.org/details/protocolbookofsi50gawa/page/36
2 CONT
2 CONT https://digital.nls.uk/dcn6/8064/80641606.6.pdf Die Septimo mensis Januarij Anno Domini quo supra—Sentencia Divorcii inter Gelis Scrymgeor et Archibaldum Dundas.—The quhilk daye in ye actione and caws of diuorce intentat be Gelis 
2 CONC Scrimgeour a^anis Archebald Dundas hyr husband for ye fylthy crym of adultry committed be hym with Anne Duncane and Catren Cragdenny as desyr of this term set to pronunce The superintendent awysit with libellat summondis of Gelis 
2 CONC answer of Archebald fyndis ye adulterie confessit be Archebald And heirfor pronuncis and with ye awys and consall of ye ministrie decernis ye said Archebald an adulterar and yarfor accord- yng to ye law of God ye sayd Gelis Scrymg
2 CONC eour separated and diuor- ciat fra hym with liberte to hyr in ye Lord to marie ony other man ac- cording to ye law of God and ye said Archebald be supplicacion to hi committed in ye handis of his magistrat quhom to he is subiect v
2 CONC idz. ye Bailie of Abyrnethe and Peter Dundas is becumin caucion for Archebald his father yat he sail compeir befoyr ye said Bailie and vnderly ciuil cor- rectione for ye foyrsaidis crimes according to ordor resauit.
