1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The research of Carol Reichus linked him to a Danish divinity student named “Andreas Andreæ Rincopius”. As one needed a degree from the University of Copenhagen to become a priest in Norway at the time,  Anders And
2 CONC erson had to had that degree. The research of Jarle Møen finds that only one of the three “Andreas Andreæ Rincopius” in the inscription lists at https://dis-danmark.dk/bibliotek/800179.pdf  seems to fit. The third Andreas who was 
2 CONC enrolled in 1647 and did his entrance exam in Ribe (thus known as "Riber' perhaps)
2 CONT
2 CONT The following is translated from the "Gards- og ættesoge for Eidfjord"
2 CONT
2 CONT Anders Anderson Riber (about 1625-1688). Married in 1657 to Katrina Helvig Lauritsdtr. Galtung (1635-1693).
2 CONT
2 CONT He was unknown in Eidfjord before he came from Jylland, Denmark. In Eidfjord he soon became a popular person as he lived like a farmer amongst farmers, and he was a   great preacher. He owned many farms, and parts of more farms. A
2 CONC fter his death, Katrina lived for the rest of her life at their farm, Lægreid Nedre, "Prestegarden" (which it's still called today).
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT - Lars (1658-1709) was a sheriff in Graven (Ulvik)
2 CONT
2 CONT - Mette m 1694 to Mikael Jonasson Rosen, Strand in Ryfylke.
2 CONT
2 CONT - Anders (1663-?), Hereid in Eidfjord.
2 CONT
2 CONT - Johannes (?-1730) worked in the church in Graven, m 1695 to Sara Jensdtr., Fryste.
2 CONT
2 CONT - Anna Katrina (1665-?) m 1689 to Hans Olson Audneland (or Brekke), Ulvik. Of their five children, two of the daughters lived in Eidfjord:
2 CONT
2 CONT --- Katrina Helvig was m to Torstein Olson Sygnestveit, Hereid.
2 CONT
2 CONT --- Elisabet Maria was m to Nils Olmodson Garatun, Garatun.
2 CONT
2 CONT - Elisabet Maria (?-1693), unmarried.
2 CONT
2 CONT - Per (1676-1721), Hereid.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT He was ordinated to priest in Eidfjord in 1656
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Fra Ribe i Danmark, Jylland
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.genealogi.no/prester-i-hardanger-prosti/
2 CONT
2 CONT Anders Andersen Riber was a famous preacher in his day and
2 CONT
2 CONT *Died 13 apr. 1688, Eidfjord i Hardanger, Langfredag 1688.
2 CONT
2 CONT *According to Kaldsbrevet, Riber was employed as a parish priest for Eidfjord's Kald in Hardanger in 1656, where he remained for his death Good Friday 1688. He was from Jutland in Denmark, last priest in the Call and by whose reti
2 CONC rement the call was laid to Ulvik.
2 CONT
2 CONT *Skifte 1690:According to Skiftebrevet af 1690 , they had the following children: Laurits, Johannes, Anna Katarina, Anders, Peder, Elisebet Maria, Mætta .. havde de følgende Børn: Laurits, Johannes, Anna Katarina, Anders, Peder, E
2 CONC lisebet Maria, Mætta..
2 CONT
2 CONT * http://www.nose.dk/Norge/riber2.html 
2 CONT
2 CONT * http://www.nose.dk
2 CONT
2 CONT *Anders Andersen Rieber #1719 born Ribe Jylland, ref: K5 299 JO 704, Sogneprest, married Katrina Helvig Lauritsdtr (galte) 1657,born 1635, Torsnes Hardanger,  died 1693, Eidsfjord, Su1 74, T Eidsfjord. Anders died 1688, Su1 74, T 
2 CONC Eidsfjord. Sogneprest i Eidfjord Hardanger fra 1656 til sin død Langfredag 1688 Kallet var lite, da han døde blev det slått sammen med Granviv og Ulvik og presten skulle bo i Ulvik. Han arvet meget med sin kone 
2 CONT
2 CONT * Family from the book by Mandrup D.Hjetnæs ed. 1885 and digitized here: http://da2.uib.no/cgi-win/WebBok.exe?slag=lesbok&bokid=riber
