2 FILE https://media.geni.com/p13/c2/49/2d/85/5344483ab2898898/van_der_helst_portrait_of_family_original.jpg?hash=fe9d7dc62dee666c64d8ac98d467f3bf23373599db066eb77847e3776ac0cba9.1797580799
2 FORM jpg
2 TITL Portrait of a Family by Dutch artist Bartholomeus van der Helst 1647 (see comments)
2 NOTE Portrait of a Family by Dutch artist Bartholomeus van der Helst 1647, currently at the Hermitage museum in St. Petersburg, Russia.  Although the people in the painting are reported to be “unknown”, I am convinced the couple on the
3 CONC  left are Elisabeth Sophie Anne Henningsdatter Gotz Arnisæus and Johannes Henrichsen Irgens (Jürgens), and that the couple on the right are Joachim Irgens (Jürgens), Baron von Westervick and his future wife Cornelia Bicker.  The b
3 CONC oy is probably Elisabeth and Johannes' oldest child Henning Irgens who would have been about 9 or 10 years old in 1647.  Bartholomeus van der Helst is known to have painted the portrait of Cornelia Bicker's father Andries Bicker, 
3 CONC heer van Engelenburg, mayor of Amsterdam and her mother Trijn Jansdr Gansneb Tengnagel.  Van der Helst also painted the portrait of Cornelia Bicker's brother Gerard Bicker.  The known portrait of  Trijn Jansdr Gansneb Tengnagel lo
3 CONC oks strikingly similar to the portrait of the woman I have identified as her daughter Cornelia Bicker in this painting in both dress and facial features. Johannes and Elisabeth Sophie Arnisæus Irgens also had their own portrait pa
3 CONC inted by an unknown artist probably in Amsterdam sometime between 1660-1670 that now hangs in the church at Røros.  The facial features are consistent in both paintings right down to the mole on Johannes' face beside his nose. Als
3 CONC o the common motif of angels or cherubs in the clouds on both portraits cannot be ignored.  Restoration of the Røros painting was completed in 2001 and x-rays revealed that an earlier version of Elisabeth Sophie had been painted o
3 CONC ver sometime prior to its installation at the church.  The apparel Elisabeth Sophie was wearing in the initial portrait looked very similar to the garments worn in the van der Helst family portrait.----Don Pirius 1 May 2013.
