1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Hugh, became captain in one of the Scots regiments in the service of Holland on 20th September, 1/29, and lieut.-general in 17/2. As a special mark of honour he was made honorary colonel of his grandfather's old re
2 CONC giment of Scots, 1/th December, 1773 (Scots Brigade in Holland, ii., 122). He m. Isabella de Savornin, and d. at Breda 9th July, 1775, leaving issue an only dau. of whom follows : —
2 CONT
2 CONT Anna Louisa Mackay, m. Lieut.-General Prevost, colonel of the 60th Foot, and Lord of Belsinge in the Republic of Genoa. On the 5th September, 1775, General Prevost "obtained his Majesty's Royal Licence and authority for himself an
2 CONC d his issue by his wife Anne Louisa, to assume and take the surname of Mackay, and also to bear the arms of Mackay of Scoury in the shire of Sutherland, pursuant to the will of Hugh Mackay of Scoury, Escpr., deceased at Breda, lat
2 CONC e lieut.-general and colonel of his Majesty's regiment of Infantry in the service of the States General" (London Gazette, September, 1775, and Blk. MS.). They had issue :—
2 CONT * James Mackay-Prevost, lieut.-general in the 60th Foot, 19th August, 1777; and
2 CONT *  two daus.
2 CONT
2 CONT pg. 291 THE BOOK OF MACKAY BY ANGUS MACKAY, M.A. (St. Andrews University)
